WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:02.490
- [Narrator] The subtlety of art depends

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:03.971
on the artist's ability to deliver

00:00:03.971 --> 00:00:07.640
their message in a single brushstroke.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.280
With 50 years of experience
studying and practicing

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.461
traditional Korean calligraphy,

00:00:12.461 --> 00:00:16.221
artist Huh Hwe-Tae has
subtlety transformed Hangul

00:00:16.221 --> 00:00:18.851
into a universal language
by blending emotion

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:23.018
and calligraphy into a new
art form called Emography.

00:00:29.051 --> 00:00:32.718
(speaking foreign language)

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.486
- [Narrator] In 2005, Master
Huh created Emography.

00:00:49.486 --> 00:00:54.450
He begins his process by
finding inspiration in nature

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:58.200
and also in the subtleties
of Korean culture.

00:01:00.581 --> 00:01:03.609
Master Huh envisions which
characters he'll use to tell

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:06.851
his story and channels his
emotions into his brush.

00:01:06.851 --> 00:01:09.601
(drumming music)

00:01:12.203 --> 00:01:15.288
Master Huh uses hanji ranging in size,

00:01:15.288 --> 00:01:18.089
often over six feet in length.

00:01:18.089 --> 00:01:20.563
Using his enormous horse hair brush,

00:01:20.563 --> 00:01:23.971
Master Huh quickly moves
from one side to the other

00:01:23.971 --> 00:01:26.064
creating a giant picture comprised

00:01:26.064 --> 00:01:28.397
of lines both big and small.

00:01:29.661 --> 00:01:32.443
The messages Master Huh
creates are designed to read

00:01:32.443 --> 00:01:35.899
as Korean letters, but
subtly appear as images that

00:01:35.899 --> 00:01:40.283
can be universally understood
outside of Korean culture.

00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:44.363
In this piece, Master Huh
writes the Korean word for seed.

00:01:44.363 --> 00:01:46.139
Looking deeper at the piece,

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.072
the letters subtly transform into

00:01:48.072 --> 00:01:50.905
a landscape with trees and plants.

00:01:51.739 --> 00:01:55.051
Each of Master Huh's works
combines letters and imagery

00:01:55.051 --> 00:01:58.461
that represent beauty,
Korean and Western traditions

00:01:58.461 --> 00:02:00.643
and the power of nature.

00:02:00.643 --> 00:02:03.632
Without speaking, Master
Huh is able to communicate

00:02:03.632 --> 00:02:05.861
these experiences to his audiences

00:02:05.861 --> 00:02:09.490
as a sensual and emotional form of art.

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:13.240
(speaking foreign language)

